WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.060
Good morning, Hank.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.060
It's Monday, September 12th.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.060
My posters have arrived!

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.839
So yesterday I took a walk in the woods with
Henry and the Yeti.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.190
Henry and I practiced words.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.430
John: Will you say tractor?

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.440
Henry: Tractor.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.470
John: Can you say nerd?

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.470
Henry: Nerd.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:13.470
John: Fighter?

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.470
Henry: [mumbles]

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:15.480
John: Pretty good.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.480
Can you say happy?

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.480
Henry: Happy!

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:20.259
So we walked down to the white river and for
the longest time Henry just stood there and

00:00:20.259 --> 00:00:21.859
watched the water flow downstream.

00:00:21.859 --> 00:00:24.039
I think he was trying to figure it out.

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:25.810
Like, what is this made out of?

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:26.810
What does it do?

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.520
Why does it always go in the same direction?

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.119
Anyway, we stayed down there for a long time
and then we went to a playground.

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:35.010
For me, September 11th is always a good day
to spend with family because I am always reminded

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.610
on that day that we're only here for a little
while.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.610
That we only have so long to play in the dirt
and ask questions of rivers.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.180
Hank, it seems to me that one of the points
of being alive is that we get to pay attention.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.410
We get to both participate in and observe
this weird universe that is simultaneously,

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.120
like, stunningly elegant and completely heartless.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.810
Clone: Just like all your ex-girlfriends.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:59.570
Oh come on, you can't just like zoom in, make
a joke and vroom out.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.570
That's rude, okay?

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.740
I am trying to make a moving point here, this
is not a jokey-joke video.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:04.740
Go back to signing!

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.679
So Hank, some nerdfighters were put off by
your video on Friday.

00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:10.380
They felt like you didn't talk about 9/11
directly enough, or with enough seriousness.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.990
I definitely found your video much less offensive
than say, Budweiser's 9/11 commercials, but

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:17.140
there was something weird about it, and yesterday
while I was walking in the woods with Henry

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.890
and the Yeti, I kept thinking about it.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.329
And eventually I started thinking about maps.

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:24.280
Like if you want to render the planet in two
dimensions, you are forced to distort it.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.880
You have to pick north is up, or north is
down.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.119
You have to squeeze the continents this way,
or this way, or this way.

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:32.240
All year long we've been talking about how
the truth resists simplicity.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.649
Hank, I agree with everything you said about
memory and 9/11 and terror, but like any map

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:38.619
it was distorted and insufficient.

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:42.560
So was my map last week about the Great Gatsby,
but the 9/11 map is much more, like, emotionally

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.790
and psychologically charged.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:46.249
But Hank, I want to make something clear to
you and to Nerdfighteria.

00:01:46.249 --> 00:01:50.630
The maps that we make with our vlogbrothers
videos will always be distorted and insufficient,

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.969
but the great thing about Nerdfighteria is
that Hank and I are not the only nerdfighters.

00:01:55.969 --> 00:01:59.880
There are thousands of us working together
to build the best, most accurate maps we can

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:00.950
collectively draw.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.959
What's interesting and important about online
communities in general, and Nerdfighteria

00:02:03.959 --> 00:02:09.090
in particular, is that this community works
to improve and enhance our maps through youtube

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:13.349
comments and on twitter and on tumblr and
at the ning and in Your Pants when they aren't

00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:15.530
hacked, which, unfortunately they still are,
sorry about that.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:16.530
We're working on it.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.830
And ideally together as a community we end
up making better maps than any of us could

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:20.830
make alone.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.180
We call each other to pay attention.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.141
In short, Nerdfighteria, we're in the business
of reminding each other to be awesome, and

00:02:26.141 --> 00:02:28.560
I would argue that business is good.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.210
Hank, I will see-- Wait!

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.040
I forgot about North Carolina!

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.520
Mom's going to kill me if I don't mention
North Carolina.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.370
Hank, next month I will be speaking and signing
in Ashville, North Carolina as a fundraiser

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.010
for my parents' hometown library.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.150
All the proceeds will go to the library.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.329
Tickets are ten bucks, there's more info in
the dooblydoo.

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:45.329
Okay, Hank.

00:02:45.329 --> 00:02:46.340
Now, I will see you on Wednesday.

